# (1.4.2, the user's: "too much lag between the end of one piece and the start of the next"; build/design/REPORT-mixgap.txt)
# A Set's hand-over without a hole: the music never more than 12 LU under its main for longer than about a bar
# (trhole, ms: the longest stretch of the momentary loudness, K-weighted, under the main's 16 s before the outro by 12
# LU, from the outro to the next piece's bar 8); the short-term loudness there never far under it (trlow, LU x10) nor
# over it (trswell: Fog's held echo swelled 12 LU over its main). Before the fix: Concrete into Night Drive trhole 2100,
# trlow -154; Fog into Concrete trswell 121; the outro called in Pressure's intro (the Songs sheet's take) trhole
# 25100, its hand-over 76 s after PLAY; Pressure into Haze, Segue, trhole 3800
listen
wait 1500
tap PLAY
wait 1500
# 1. short 61: Concrete (136; Intro None, Main 32 bars, Outro 16) into Night Drive (120), Mix
turn PRESET 4 5
wait 800
expect piece 4
tap GLO
wait 300
tap GLO
wait 300
expect view 28
spin K1 2
wait 300
spin K2 2
wait 300
expect par158 2
expect trans 2
tap HOME
wait 300
tap HOME
wait 300
expect view 27
spin K1 -16
spin K2 -16
spin K3 -2
wait 300
expect par159 0
expect par160 4
expect par161 2
tap PLAY
wait 300
trwatch
# the downbeat at about 86 s, Night Drive's bar 8 at 102
wait 104000
expect piece 5
expect trrestarts 1
expect trhole <2100
expect trlow >-120
expect trswell <60
expect trkick <2
# (Night Drive from its second phrase: its bass at 6.4 bars, not 14.5; its kick one and three from the downbeat)
expect trbass >15
expect trbass <130
expect trchord >31
expect trdip 0
expect trjump <10
# (Concrete's stab struck two bars before the end reads 211 here, before the fix as after: its own sharp edge)
expect trclick <250
tap PLAY
wait 500
expect playing 0
# 2. Fog (120; the same lengths) into Concrete (136), Mix: its held echo no longer swells over the music
turn PRESET -2
wait 800
expect piece 3
tap GLO
wait 300
tap GLO
wait 300
expect view 28
tap HOME
wait 300
tap HOME
wait 300
expect view 27
spin K1 -16
spin K2 -16
spin K3 -2
wait 300
expect par159 0
expect par160 4
expect par161 2
tap PLAY
wait 300
trwatch
wait 111000
expect piece 4
expect trrestarts 1
expect trswell <60
expect trhole <2100
expect trlow >-120
expect trclick <80
tap PLAY
wait 500
expect playing 0
# 3. the Songs sheet's take: Pressure as it is (Intro 32 bars, Main 160, Outro 32), the outro called in its intro's
# bar 3, when only the kick and the bass are in: the outro as long as the intro had been (8 bars, from bar 8), the
# kick to the end, the chord thrown into the held echo all the same; Haze's downbeat at bar 16 (about 31 s), not 76 s
turn PRESET 2
wait 800
expect piece 6
expect par159 4
expect par161 4
tap PLAY
wait 300
trwatch
wait 5000
press HOME
wait 300
tap PLAY
wait 300
release HOME
wait 22000
expect piece 6
wait 6000
expect piece 7
expect playing 1
expect trrestarts 1
wait 15000
expect trhole <2100
expect trlow >-130
expect trkick <2
tap PLAY
wait 500
expect playing 0
# 4. Segue: Pressure (Intro None, Main 32, Outro 16) into Haze: the kick to the end, the echo held a bar longer over
# Haze's bare start (its intro from the top, as a Segue has it: by its bar 5 its own dark wash, 15-25 LU under the main)
tap GLO
wait 300
tap GLO
wait 300
expect view 28
spin K2 -1
wait 300
expect trans 1
turn PRESET -1
wait 800
expect piece 6
tap GLO
wait 300
tap GLO
wait 300
expect view 28
tap HOME
wait 300
tap HOME
wait 300
expect view 27
spin K1 -16
spin K2 -16
spin K3 -2
wait 300
expect par159 0
expect par160 4
expect par161 2
tap PLAY
wait 300
trwatch
wait 111000
expect piece 7
expect trrestarts 1
expect trhole <2500
expect trlow >-170
expect trquiet <2000
expect trclick <80
